    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T00:35:45Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">A robin’s orange breast is easiest to spot in winter: with leaves gone and food scarcer, these birds often defend feeding territories more visibly.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#027c02b94ea1b6cf94576dee0407ed84ef2e6aae89b15527368da035066f6879</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T00:35:45Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Community fridges show how a simple shared resource can prevent good food going to waste: local groups coordinate donations and let neighbours take what they need.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#f425c3c87f066c3a7fa397f3cd299430aae9f9e5657819f476fc6bbfe5330c52</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T00:35:45Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Next time you pass a library, spend three minutes checking its noticeboard for a free local event, then tell someone who might enjoy it.</div>
    </content>
